extra.final_message:
The build passes. (`git diff` was empty only because this working copy lives under a `runs/` path ignored by an outer repo — the edits are on disk and compiled into the APK.)

## Root cause

`TextInputLayout`'s `app:passwordToggleEnabled="true"` end icon is hard-wired to toggle the transformation method of the **one `EditText` it wraps**. In both `component_authentication.xml` and `component_password.xml`, only `passwordEdit` lives inside the `TextInputLayout`; `passwordConfirm` is a sibling `EditText` outside it. So the built-in toggle could never reach the confirmation field.

`IntroScreenActivity` had already worked around this (the fix for #580) by overriding the end-icon click listener and fanning the change out to both fields — but that fix was written inline in the intro fragment, so settings never got it.

## The fix

**1. `Utilities/UIHelper.java`** — new shared helper that owns the behavior:

```java
public static void setupPasswordVisibilityToggle(final TextInputLayout passwordLayout,
                                                 final EditText passwordInput,
                                                 final EditText passwordConfirm) {
    passwordLayout.setEndIconOnClickListener(new View.OnClickListener() {
        @Override
        public void onClick(View v) {
            boolean wasHidden = passwordInput.getTransformationMethod() instanceof PasswordTransformationMethod;

            // Dispatch the visibility change to both the password and the confirmation input
            dispatchPasswordVisibilityChange(passwordInput, wasHidden);
            dispatchPasswordVisibilityChange(passwordConfirm, wasHidden);

            passwordLayout.refreshDrawableState();
        }
    });

    passwordInput.setTransformationMethod(PasswordTransformationMethod.getInstance());
    passwordConfirm.setTransformationMethod(PasswordTransformationMethod.getInstance());
}
```

`dispatchPasswordVisibilityChange` saves/restores `getSelectionEnd()`, since swapping the transformation method resets the cursor.

**2. `Preferences/CredentialsPreference.java`** (the reported bug — Settings → Authentication). Both the `PASSWORD` and `PIN` branches of `updateLayout()` replaced their two bare `setTransformationMethod(new PasswordTransformationMethod())` calls with `UIHelper.setupPasswordVisibilityToggle(passwordLayout, passwordInput, passwordConfirm)`. Placement is kept *after* `setInputType(...)`, which itself resets the transformation method.

**3. `Preferences/PasswordEncryptedPreference.java`** — Settings → Encryption → Password has the identical layout shape and identical defect, so it's fixed the same way.

**4. `Activities/IntroScreenActivity.java`** — its two private methods were deleted and `setPasswordTransformationMethod()` now delegates to the helper. Behavior is unchanged (the extraction is mechanical), but the intro and settings paths can no longer drift apart the way they just did.

Two now-unused `PasswordTransformationMethod` imports were dropped.

## Result

Tapping the visibility icon in the Authentication dialog now reveals/masks **both** the PIN/Password field and its confirmation field together, matching the intro screen, with the toggle icon state and cursor positions preserved.
